pe` when printing. This will then append a sequence after every emoji to ensure that the correct variation is printed. See the `emoji` package [code in action](https://github.com/carpedm20/emoji/blob/70e7ba12dfaf3449a5d445b1e7de4ae2c6245d19/ ...\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a9f792a6-fead-4ce7-8fab-71bea99b362e","uuid":"900cd66d-f726-4ae4-8551-17dc097b598a","timestamp":"2026-10-27T06:45:41.278Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"searched_issues\": 1537,\n  \"quarantined\": 0,\n  \"threshold\": 0.35,\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"number\": 3117,\n      \"score\": 0.261,\n      \"title\": \"[BUG] Panel inside Layout being cut off\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"strong\": false,\n      \"excerpt\": \"- [x] I've checked [docs](https://rich.readthedocs.io/en/latest/introduction.html) and [closed issues](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aclosed) for possible solutions. - [x] I can't find my issue in the [FAQ](https://github.com/Textualize/rich/blob/master/FAQ.md). **Describe the bug** When rendering a panel inside a layout the content of the panel is cut short. The bottom border of the panel is still drawen. When printing the panel itself everything appears good. Note below render group can be replaced with a big string that would take up a lot of the terminal ```pyt ...\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 3520,\n      \"score\": 0.238,\n      \"title\": \"[REQUEST] Strip emoji shortcodes on emoji=False\",\n      \"state\": \"open\",\n      \"state_reason\": null,\n      \"strong\": false,\n      \"excerpt\": \"Have you checked the issues for a similar suggestions? Yes **How would you improve Rich?** Propose on Console to strip emoji (strip shortcodes before rendering) if emoji is False. Also add an options to if the user want to strip emoji or keep the emoji. Here this the code inherit from Console that strip emoji if emoji is False: ```pyt